---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../lib/seo/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How TextFixer handles privacy for browser-based text tools."
  canonicalPath="/privacy"
>
  <article class="container-page max-w-3xl py-12 prose-privacy">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: August 27, 2026</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Summary</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      {SITE_NAME} is designed so that normal text tools process your content locally in your browser.
      We do not require an account to use the tools.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Local processing</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      For tools that run entirely in the browser (including Text Cleaner), your input text is not
      uploaded to a {SITE_NAME} server for processing. Processing happens on your device using
      client-side code.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">What we may store on your device</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      We may use <code class="rounded bg-surface-2 px-1">localStorage</code> for non-sensitive preferences
      such as theme (light/dark). We do not store your tool input or output in localStorage by default.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Analytics</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      If analytics are enabled in the future, we intend to track anonymous product events such as which
      tools are opened or run. We will not send the contents of your input, output, extracted emails,
      phone numbers, URLs, JSON, or HTML to analytics.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Advertising</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      The site may display advertisements in the future. Ad partners may use cookies or similar
      technologies according to their own policies. Ads will not be designed to look like tool controls.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      Privacy questions: see our <a class="text-accent underline" href="/contact">contact page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-muted">
      If future features require server-side processing, we will isolate them and update this policy to
      match the actual architecture.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
